==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|jibe}}

===Etymology===
From obsolete {{etyl|nl|en}} {{m|nl|gijben}} (modern Dutch: ''gijpen'').

===Verb===
{{en-verb|gyb}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} To change [[tack]] with the [[wind]] crossing behind the boat. (Mostly used of boats and other small sailing craft — the corresponding manoeuver in a sailing ship is to [[wear]].)
# {{lb|en|nautical}} To shift a fore-and-aft sail suddenly and forcefully from one side to the other, while sailing before the wind. (also [[jibe]].)
# To sneer (see [[gibe]].)
# ''gybe at'': to hesitate, vacillate, or [[balk]] when faced with a proposal, plan, or course of action. (''Obsolete'')

